### Task 1: ME link seam and the ME-first output path

**Files:**
- Create: `J/multiblock/MeStatus.java`, `J/multiblock/MeLink.java`, `J/gametest/FakeMeLink.java`, `J/gametest/MeLinkTests.java`
- Modify: `J/multiblock/OutputSink.java`, `J/blockentity/CoreBlockEntity.java` (`buildPools`), `J/gametest/MPTestRegistration.java`

**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: plan 1's `OutputSink`, `LiveBlocks`, `ExportBlockEntity.storage()`, `Multiblock.me()`.
- Produces:
  - `enum MeStatus { NONE, OFFLINE, NO_CHANNEL, ONLINE }`
  - `interface MeLink { MeStatus status(); long insertItem(ItemResource resource, long amount, boolean simulate); long extractItem(ItemResource resource, long amount, boolean simulate); long extractEnergy(long amount, boolean simulate); ItemResource fertilizerFilter(); boolean isRemoved(); default boolean online() { return status() == MeStatus.ONLINE; } }`
  - `OutputSink(List<ExportBlockEntity> inOrder, @Nullable MeLink me, Runnable onStale)`
  - `CoreBlockEntity.meStatus(): MeStatus` (NONE when the structure has no live link)
  - `FakeMeLink(MeStatus status, long capacity)` with public mutable fields `status`, `removed`, `filter` (`ItemResource`), `energy` (`long`), `modulateShortfall` (`long`, how many fewer items a real insert takes than the simulation said), and `long stored(ItemResource)`, `void put(ItemResource, long)`.

- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests in `J/gametest/MeLinkTests.java`**

Each test places one export block at `(1,1,1)` and builds the sink directly. Register the class in `MPTestRegistration.cases()` unconditionally, since it needs no AE2.

```java
private static void onlineLinkTakesOutputsFirst(GameTestHelper helper) {
    ExportBlockEntity export = placeExport(helper);
    FakeMeLink me = new FakeMeLink(MeStatus.ONLINE, 1000);
    OutputSink sink = new OutputSink(List.of(export), me, () -> {});
    helper.assertTrue(sink.insert(new ItemStack(Items.WHEAT, 64)).isEmpty(), "nothing left over");
    helper.assertValueEqual(me.stored(ItemResource.of(Items.WHEAT)), 64L, "wheat in ME");
    helper.assertValueEqual(count(export, Items.WHEAT), 0, "wheat in export");
    helper.succeed();
}

private static void offlineLinkSendsOutputsToExport(GameTestHelper helper) {
    // FakeMeLink(MeStatus.OFFLINE, 1000), insert 64 wheat
    helper.assertValueEqual(me.stored(ItemResource.of(Items.WHEAT)), 0L, "wheat in ME");
    helper.assertValueEqual(count(export, Items.WHEAT), 64, "wheat in export");
}

private static void removedLinkIsSkippedAndMarksStale(GameTestHelper helper) {
    // FakeMeLink ONLINE with removed = true, onStale sets an AtomicBoolean, insert 64 wheat
    helper.assertValueEqual(count(export, Items.WHEAT), 64, "wheat in export");
    helper.assertTrue(stale.get(), "onStale ran");
}

private static void roomCountsMeRoom(GameTestHelper helper) {
    // export filled with 54 stacks of cobblestone, FakeMeLink ONLINE with capacity 64
    helper.assertTrue(sink.hasRoomFor(List.of(new ItemStack(Items.WHEAT, 64))), "ME room counts");
    helper.assertTrue(!sink.hasRoomFor(List.of(new ItemStack(Items.WHEAT, 65))), "65 do not fit");
}

private static void mePartialRoomSendsTheRestToExport(GameTestHelper helper) {
    // FakeMeLink ONLINE with capacity 10, export empty
    List<ItemStack> drops = List.of(new ItemStack(Items.WHEAT, 64), new ItemStack(Items.WHEAT, 64));
    helper.assertTrue(sink.hasRoomFor(drops), "room");
    for (ItemStack drop : drops) {
        helper.assertTrue(sink.insert(drop.copy()).isEmpty(), "nothing left over");
    }
    helper.assertValueEqual(me.stored(ItemResource.of(Items.WHEAT)), 10L, "wheat in ME");
    helper.assertValueEqual(count(export, Items.WHEAT), 118, "wheat in export");
}
```

Register them as `online_link_takes_outputs_first`, `offline_link_sends_outputs_to_export`, `removed_link_is_skipped_and_marks_stale`, `room_counts_me_room`, `me_partial_room_sends_the_rest_to_export`, each `new TestCase(20, ...)`.

- [ ] **Step 2: Run the GameTests to verify they fail**

Run: `./gradlew runGameTestServer`
Expected: FAIL to compile, `MeLink`, `MeStatus`, `FakeMeLink` and the three-argument `OutputSink` constructor are missing.

- [ ] **Step 3: Implement `MeStatus`, `MeLink`, `FakeMeLink` and the OutputSink ME path**

- `OutputSink` gets a private `@Nullable MeLink liveMe()` that returns null when there is no link, and calls `onStale` and returns null when `me.isRemoved()`. `insert` and `hasRoomFor` send to `liveMe()` first when it is `online()`, then to the export blocks. In `hasRoomFor`, ME is asked with `simulate = true` per stack and the remainder goes into the export blocks inside the existing root transaction. Put one comment on that loop saying that ME has no transactions, so stacks that share ME room can both pass, and the part ME refuses later goes to the export blocks or is held in the planter block.
- `CoreBlockEntity.buildPools` resolves `multiblock.me()` with `level.getBlockEntity(pos) instanceof MeLink link` and passes it to the sink, keeping it in a `@Nullable MeLink me` field that is nulled wherever the pools are nulled. `meStatus()` returns `MeStatus.NONE` when `me` is null or removed, else `me.status()`.
- `FakeMeLink` caps the total of all items at `capacity` and takes `modulateShortfall` fewer items on a real insert than a simulated one, never below 0. `extractItem` and `extractEnergy` return at most what it holds, and a simulated call changes nothing. Every method returns 0 unless `status` is `ONLINE`.

- [ ] **Step 4: Run the GameTests to verify they pass**

Run: `./gradlew runGameTestServer`
Expected: exits 0, the five new tests pass, and every plan 1 test still passes.

- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**

```bash
git add src/main/java/io/github/julianperge/modular_planters/multiblock src/main/java/io/github/julianperge/modular_planters/blockentity/CoreBlockEntity.java src/main/java/io/github/julianperge/modular_planters/gametest
git commit -m "feat: send outputs to an online me link before the export blocks"
```

